This is a regression test for an issue that was resulting in crashes in a
number of places (gh#117).

When opening a currently hidden output buffer we should correctly focus that
buffer in the layout state and future inputs should be sent to the correct
buffer.

-- config --
path: tests/data/config/without-fsys.toml
-- file-foo.txt --
foo
-- file-bar.txt --
bar
-- file-baz.txt --
baz
-- actions --
# ls should open the output buffer
type: !ls\n
sleep_ms: 100

# we then close it and run ls again to trigger the bug. Annoyingly this is racey thanks
# to the async command execution so we have a couple of additional keystrokes spaced out
# with sleeps in order to ensure we have the output (and layout changes) from the second
# call to ls
type: :delete-window\n
type: !ls\n
sleep_ms: 100
type: j
sleep_ms: 100
type: j
sleep_ms: 100

# this delete should run in the output buffer: we use Alt-j to select the second
# instance of baz for deletion.
type: /baz
type: <alt>j
type: \nxd
-- buffer-list --
1      foo.txt
2      bar.txt
3      baz.txt
4    * +output
-- expected-windows --
3
4
-- expected-buffer-3 --
baz
-- expected-buffer-4 --
bar.txt
baz.txt
foo.txt
bar.txt
foo.txt

